. *******************************************************************
. * Attrition tests, specific to regressions
. *******************************************************************
. 
. * We run two attrition tests to assess attrition bias
. * 1) Regress attrition on the dose groups and on the binary drought
. * 2) Baseline Outcomes of Attrited and Non-Attrited Children
.         *(a) regress the 2005 outcome on attrition for all children
.         *(b) keep only the children lost to attrition and regress their 2005 
> outcome on the treatment
. * NOTE: One row per child the 2005 row, no fixed effects or controls like the
>  balance table, standard errors clustered by 2005 municipality
. 
. 
. *** ATTRITION CONCEPT ******
.     * NOTE: CAN THINK OF DID AS DENOMINATOR AND ATTRITED AS NUMERATOR
.     * attrited = 1: the child met the sample rules in 2005 and would still ha
> ve been young enough in 2009, but has no usable 2009 measurement, so the chil
> d dropped out of the sample
.     * attrited = 0: the child was measured in 2009 and is in the regression s
> ample. Children who simply aged out aren't counted either way
. 
. 
. foreach o in haz waz bmiz {
  2.     * did = 1 marks every child who met the DID sample rules in 2005 and c
> ould have been in the 2009 estimation sample
.     gen did = (year == 2005 & age < `cut_`o'' & !missing(`o') & !missing(trea
> t2009) & treat_early == 0 & age_next < `cut_`o'')
  3.     * Attrited = 1 if the child is not in the 2009 estimation sample and 0
>  if the child is. Both are eligible children, i.e. did == 1 in both cases
.     gen attrited = (reg_`o' != 1) if did == 1
  4.     * Test 1, dose groups vs near normal and binary drought
.     quietly regress attrited cls_mod cls_sev if did == 1, vce(cluster cvegeo0
> 5)
  5.         * Computes mean attrition
.     quietly summarize attrited if e(sample)
  6.     estadd scalar mean = r(mean)
  7.     eststo a1_`o'
  8.     quietly regress attrited treat2009 if did == 1, vce(cluster cvegeo05)
  9.     quietly summarize attrited if e(sample)
 10.     estadd scalar mean = r(mean)
 11.     eststo a2_`o'
 12.     * Test 2 (a) the 2005 outcome on attrition for all children on the dos
> e sample and the binary sample
.     quietly regress `o' attrited if did == 1 & !missing(cls_mod), vce(cluster
>  cvegeo05)
 13.     quietly summarize `o' if e(sample)
 14.     estadd scalar mean = r(mean)
 15.     eststo b1_`o'
 16.     quietly regress `o' attrited if did == 1, vce(cluster cvegeo05)
 17.     quietly summarize `o' if e(sample)
 18.     estadd scalar mean = r(mean)
 19.     eststo b2_`o'
 20.     * Test 2 (b) only the children lost to attrition. Their 2005 outcome o
> n the dose groups and on the binary drought
.     quietly regress `o' cls_mod cls_sev if did == 1 & attrited == 1, vce(clus
> ter cvegeo05)
 21.     quietly summarize `o' if e(sample)
 22.     estadd scalar mean = r(mean)
 23.     eststo c1_`o'
 24.     quietly regress `o' treat2009 if did == 1 & attrited == 1, vce(cluster
>  cvegeo05)
 25.     quietly summarize `o' if e(sample)
 26.     estadd scalar mean = r(mean)
 27.     eststo c2_`o'
 28.     drop did attrited
 29. }
